/* ============================================================
   NO MALARKEY — govern-phase engine (Q1–Q14)
   Source: scenario bible v0.9 + drafted questions doc.
   Tally tiers per bible §2; FX blocks per the doc's A-lines.

   v0.9 calibration, applied here:
     - delivery-write rule (§2.1, extended by §D): every answer carries a
       declared outcome class — loss -1, partial 0, win +1, a win through a
       record-gated branch +2, an RNG win a flat +1 — whether or not its
       question carries a result flag. The rule used to derive the class from
       the flag, so the flagless questions fell straight through it; Q7 A4,
       Q11 A1 and Q12 A3 all paid a win's grant for a partial and now pay 0.
     - floor_safe (§B): the best delivery an *accumulator-blind* player can
       hold — one who never picks an answer that branches on delivery(prior)
       or on an RNG roll. It is the second input to every gate and is carried
       beside the ceiling in the ledger from now on.
     - gate ladder re-anchored (§E) on floor_safe(n) + floor(gap(n) / 2), where
       gap = ceiling - floor_safe: Q8 >= +3, Q9 >= +4, Q12 >= +7, Q13 >= +7
       (>= +5 with midterm_push), Q14 >= +8. Q7 stays >= +1 as a declared
       exemption. See NM_GATE for why the v0.8 half-ceiling ladder could not
       have worked at any numerals.
     - midterm_push repriced (§G): the Q13 discount is 2 points, not 1. At 1 it
       exactly cancelled the delivery Q11 A3 gives up against its siblings, so
       the flag was worth precisely zero from the day it was introduced.
     - midterm_result (§K): Q13 gets the standard win/partial/loss flag, so the
       write rule derives its grants like every other question's instead of
       leaving them hand-set and internally inconsistent.
     - rec_progressive still clamps at +-3 (§2); every other Tier A axis is +-2.

   Ledger after the above (§F), reproduced by an exhaustive walk of the phase:

       read         ceiling   floor   floor_safe
       Q7  A2          +3      -3        +3
       Q8  A2          +4      -4        +3
       Q9  A3          +6      -5        +3
       Q12 A4          +9      -6        +5
       Q13 A2/A3       +9      -6        +5
       Q14 A2         +11      -8        +6
       end of govern  +13      -9        +8

   §A's three desyncs are desyncs in the *document*, not here: the mod has only
   ever carried one favreau_senate block and has gated it at hosts_burned >= 2
   since v0.8, Q7 A2 has no dangling fourth branch (see case 8102), and its
   terminal test is already `rec_foreign >= 2` and not an equality. Nothing to
   apply; §A.3's prerequisite for §L is satisfied on this side. §C adds a
   fourth of the same kind, and that one WAS live — see case 8163.

   Deliberately NOT in this pass:
     - §H, rec_progressive saturation. The axis rails by Q2-Q3, not Q6-Q8, so
       Q13 A1's >= +1 and Q14 A3's >= +2 are close to free. The bible holds the
       fix back explicitly: two difficulty levers moving together is how v0.8
       produced a result nobody could attribute. Land this, play it, then move
       the axis.
     - §I, the two dominated answers (Q8 A3, Q9 A2). Q8 A3's proposed fix is a
       delivery +1, which would raise floor_safe and re-derive the whole ladder
       — so it belongs with §H, not here. Both are marked at their case below.
     - §L, the freed immigration slot. Still undrafted, and gated on §A.3.
     - Q14 Immigration is drafted and locked (§6); The Ticket (Q15) is specced
       but undrafted, so the govern phase still ends at Q14.
   ============================================================ */

