/* Favreau Senate addendum (doc, end of Q13). Gate per bible §5:
     hosts_burned >= 2 AND rec_progressive <= -3
   v0.7's threshold of 3 required the unique maximal burn path (hosts_burned
   tops out at exactly 3: Q1 A3 + Q3a A2 + one of Q12 A2 / Q12 A4-fail), which
   hard-gated the secret path on the Q2 healthcare route. Lowering it to 2 opens
   several combinations.

   The second condition does NOT do the independent work §5 claimed for it, and
   §H.3 is where that fell over. The argument was that on the widened +-3 clamp,
   reaching -3 takes at least one further moderate move beyond the burns. It
   does not: Q1 A3 and Q2 A4 alone put a player at -2 and any third moderate
   write rails them, which on a twelve-source axis is nothing to arrange. The
   moderate floor is close to a freebie here for the same reason Q13 A1's >= +1
   and Q14 A3's >= +2 are. Fixing it is §H's job — the widening moved the rail
   by about one question, not the six §9.8 assumed — and §H is deliberately not
   in this pass, so the threshold stands as-is and this comment is the record. */
var NM_FAVREAU_GATE = { hosts_burned_min: 2, progressive_max: -3 };

/* Gate ladder (bible v0.9 §E.1): each delivery(prior) gate sits at

       floor_safe(n) + floor((ceiling(n) - floor_safe(n)) / 2)

   — half the distance between the best risk-free position and the best
   possible one. Clearing a gate therefore takes roughly one successful reach
   beyond safe play, and the number of reaches grows as the phase goes on.

   v0.8 anchored on the ceiling alone, and that could not have worked at any
   numerals (§B.3): the free +1s are spread evenly across the phase, so the
   risk-free line rises at about half the ceiling's slope. The two curves are
   near parallel, and a half-ceiling gate lands on the risk-free line however
   it is tuned. Anchoring at both ends is what fixes it — a new delivery source
   now moves the gate differently depending on whether it is free or risky,
   which is exactly the discrimination the old rule lacked.

       gate   floor_safe   ceiling   gap   sits at   cheapest clearing route
       Q8         +3         +4       1      +3      perfect safe play, no reach
       Q9         +3         +6       3      +4      the above + one reach
       Q12        +5         +9       4      +7      floor_safe + Q8 A2 win
       Q13        +5         +9       4      +7      same
       Q14        +6        +11       5      +8      same, +6 already counting
                                                     Q13 A1 — still one reach

   Q8's is the only gate clearable without a reach, deliberately: at that
   position there is nothing to reach for yet. It is the last gate that tests
   avoiding failure; from Q9 on they test succeeding at risk.

   Two of §E's reachability notes do not survive measurement, and the numerals
   above are right in both cases — it is the prose under them that is off:

     - §E.3 calls Q14 "the only two-reach gate in the mod", counting a Q8 A2
       win and a Q13 A2 win. floor_safe at Q14 is +6 and that already includes
       Q13 A1's free +1, so the Q8 A2 win alone lands exactly on +8. Q14 is a
       one-reach gate, like Q12 and Q13. §13's playtest note singles it out on
       the strength of the two-reach claim; Q12 remains the sharper target,
       since it jumps three points and its failure branch feeds hosts_burned.
     - §G says the 2-point discount lets a cautious player clear Q13 without a
       reach, because +5 "lands exactly on floor_safe". It does not follow:
       floor_safe +5 is measured on a line that spends Q11 on A4's +1, and
       taking A3 to bank the flag is what gives that point up. The blind push
       line tops out at +4 — one short. The flag's net +1 is real, but the
       bargain as described needs a 3-point discount, which would contradict
       §G's own "net value: +1". Left at 2, since that is the stated numeral.

   Recompute the whole ladder if a new delivery source is ever added. */
var NM_GATE = {
    /* Q7 is a declared exemption from the rule above, not a gate derived by it.
       gap is 0 there — floor_safe and the ceiling are both +3 — so the rule
       returns +3, which would be simultaneously maximally demanding and
       completely free. It is incoherent because there is nothing yet to be
       demanding about: no answer before Q7 trades risk for delivery, so there
       is no record to discriminate on (§B.4). >= +1 does a different and
       legitimate job — it separates a player who has actively failed
       (healthcare loss, Q4 A3, Q6 A1) from one who has not. Document it as a
       failure check. The exemption ends if the freed slot lands early and
       brings the front half its first delivery risk (§L). */
    q7_failure_check: 1,
    q8_strong: 3,
    q9_confirmed: 4,
    q12_viral: 7,
    q13_hold: 7,
    q14_muscle: 8,
    /* midterm_push's discount on the Q13 gate (§G). Q11 A3 pays delivery 0
       where its siblings pay +1, so taking it costs a point. At a 1-point
       discount the flag bought back exactly that point and nothing else —
       gate >= +4 holding X is the same position as gate >= +5 holding X + 1 —
       and it was strictly worse if the player then took a Q13 answer that does
       not read it, or needed the point at Q14. It was mechanically null for
       two revisions. At 2 the flag is worth net +1. See the note above on why
       it does not also buy a reach-free clear of Q13. */
    q13_push_discount: 2
};

/* Q13 A2/A3's gate, in full: the tally band OR the midterm_push relief band.
   Both halves are the gate. Documenting it as its simple half ">= +7" is the
   §J violation — a compound gate written up as one of its branches is worse
   than a wrong numeral, because the player has no way to learn the relief
   branch exists at all. Any prose label for this node reads
   ">= +7, or >= +5 with a midterm push". */
function nmQ13Hold() {
    return nm.delivery >= NM_GATE.q13_hold
        || (nm.midterm_push && nm.delivery >= NM_GATE.q13_hold - NM_GATE.q13_push_discount);
}

function nmFavreauSenate() {
    if (NM_FAVREAU_GATE.hosts_burned_min === null) return false;
    if (NM_FAVREAU_GATE.progressive_max === null) return false;
    return nm.hosts_burned >= NM_FAVREAU_GATE.hosts_burned_min
        && nm.rec_progressive <= NM_FAVREAU_GATE.progressive_max;
}

